            TIP("Link each group to its text: women with CEDAW (1979), children with the CRC (1989) and the African Charter on the Rights and Welfare of the Child (1990). Keep to general statements and check the current rules for Cameroonian laws.", title="Exam link"),
            H("Common mistakes"),
            MISTAKE("Saying special protection means special privileges", "It aims at equal enjoyment of rights by groups that face obstacles."),
            MISTAKE("Mixing up the conventions", "CEDAW is about women; the CRC and the African Charter on the Rights and Welfare of the Child are about children."),
            MISTAKE("Thinking that protecting children means punishing all child work", "Light household help that does not harm schooling or health is different from exploitative labour that does."),
            QUIZ("Which text deals with discrimination against women?", ["The Convention on the Rights of the Child", "CEDAW", "The Geneva Conventions", "The African Charter on the Rights and Welfare of the Child"], 1,
                 "CEDAW, adopted in 1979, is the convention on the elimination of discrimination against women.",
                 hint="The first letter stands for Convention on the Elimination of Discrimination...",
                 feedback=["That concerns children.", "", "These concern war.", "That concerns children in Africa."]),
            QUIZ("What does the principle of the 'best interests of the child' mean?", ["The child decides everything alone", "Decisions about a child must put the child's well-being first", "Parents have no rights", "Children can never work or play"], 1,
                 "In every decision affecting a child, the child's well-being must be a main concern.",
                 hint="Think of whose benefit comes first.",
                 feedback=["Children are heard, but adults still share responsibility.", "", "Parents keep rights and duties.", "Children also have a right to play."]),
            H("Practice questions"),
            PQ("Define discrimination and give an example against girls.", "Discrimination is treating people unfairly because of a characteristic such as sex. Example: refusing a girl the chance to go to school because she is female."),
            PQ("Name the main international texts protecting women and children.", "CEDAW (1979) for women; the Convention on the Rights of the Child (1989) and the African Charter on the Rights and Welfare of the Child (1990) for children."),
            PQ("State three rights of a child.", "Any three of: survival and health, a name and nationality, education, protection from abuse and exploitation, play and rest, and being heard."),
            PQ("Explain two ways the community can protect minorities.", "By respecting their language, culture and way of life, and by treating them equally and including them in decisions. Leaders can speak against discrimination and schools can teach respect."),
            SUM("Women, children and minorities may face obstacles in enjoying rights, so special protection aims at equality.",
                "CEDAW (1979) protects women; the CRC (1989) and the African Charter on the Rights and Welfare of the Child (1990) protect children.",
                "Common abuses include early marriage, child labour, trafficking and gender-based violence. The Constitution's preamble commits to protect minorities and indigenous populations.",
                "The State, institutions and the community all have a part to play. Check the current Cameroonian laws."),
