            T("The Board's report advises candidates to respect the instructions on the paper, to **select questions carefully**, to master examination technique, and **not to answer by merely listing points** where the question needs developed marking. It also notes that weak answers came from poor mastery of earlier work, and that candidates should revise the work of earlier forms as well as the final year.\n\n"
              "The report also says that some questions were far more popular than others. A popular question is not always an easy one: choose according to what you know, not what others pick."),
